CORE libcxx
string_view_find.cpp
--cpp20 --stdlib libc++ --object-bits 12
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ find: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR$
dropped the body of system-header function
--
libc++ (LLVM 18) std::string_view::find(char): __constexpr_memchr<const
char, char> static_asserts clang's __is_trivially_equality_comparable and
calls __builtin_char_memchr; both were unknown, so its body was dropped
and find returned nondet.
